# All of these are wired up by `pnpm setup` — you usually don't need to edit
# this file by hand. Listed here as a reference and for power users who want
# to skip the wizard.

# ─── Convex ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auto-written by `pnpm exec convex dev` on first run. Don't fill manually.
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
VITE_CONVEX_URL=
# Same as VITE_CONVEX_URL with .cloud → .site (wizard does this for you).
VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=

# ─── Better Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET lives in the Convex env (not here). Auto-generated by
# `pnpm setup`; in prod, `pnpm setup:prod` generates a fresh one.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL also lives in the Convex env; default = http://localhost:3000.

# ─── Anthropic ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY lives in the Convex env (not here).
# → Get yours: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys

# ─── Resend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RESEND_API_KEY and RESEND_FROM live in the Convex env (not here).
# → API key:        https://resend.com/api-keys
# → Verified domain: https://resend.com/domains  (use onboarding@resend.dev for dev)
#
# DEV_NOTIFY_EMAIL (optional, Convex env): if set, a notification is sent to
# this inbox each time a new user is provisioned. Leave empty to disable.
# → pnpm exec convex env set DEV_NOTIFY_EMAIL you@example.com

# ─── Google OAuth (optional, social login) ─────────────────────────────────
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET live in the Convex env (not here).
# Leave unset to ship without the Google button (it only renders when both are
# present). `pnpm setup` prompts for these in dev; `pnpm setup:prod` mirrors
# them to prod.
# → Create an OAuth client: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   Authorized redirect URI (dev):  http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
#   Authorized redirect URI (prod): https://<your-domain>/api/auth/callback/google
#   (register BOTH on the same client; see KNOWN_ISSUES.md § Google OAuth)

# ─── Sentry (optional, front-end) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Back-end (SENTRY_DSN, SENTRY_*) lives in the Convex env. Front-end DSN below
# is build-time inlined into the bundle.
# → Get yours: https://sentry.io/settings/{org}/projects/{project}/keys/
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# ─── Convex region (decide BEFORE the first `convex dev`) ──────────────────
# Create the Convex project in EU West (Ireland). Convex asks for the region
# when a project is created, and the whole deployment lives there. A region
# CANNOT be changed afterwards — switching means a new deployment plus an
# export/import migration. Also set the team's default region in the Convex
# settings so preview deployments follow.
# This is not an env var; it is a console choice with no second chance.

# ─── Object storage (candidate recordings, CVs, question media) ────────────
# S3-compatible, private bucket. Default provider: Scaleway Object Storage,
# region fr-par. These live in the Convex env, not here:
#   pnpm exec convex env set OBJECT_STORE_ENDPOINT https://s3.fr-par.scw.cloud
#   pnpm exec convex env set OBJECT_STORE_REGION fr-par
#   pnpm exec convex env set OBJECT_STORE_BUCKET interw-media
#   pnpm exec convex env set OBJECT_STORE_ACCESS_KEY_ID ...
#   pnpm exec convex env set OBJECT_STORE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY ...
# Optional, for a local MinIO that only speaks path-style addressing:
#   pnpm exec convex env set OBJECT_STORE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE true
#
# The bucket MUST be private. Nothing in this app ever reads an object without
# a signed URL minted after an access check — see convex/lib/objectStore.ts.

# ─── Erasure register salt (REQUIRED — erasure fails without it) ────────────
# `purgeLog` records that a candidate's data was destroyed, and stores a hash
# of their address rather than the address. A bare SHA-256 would not be one-way
# in any useful sense: the input space is a list of addresses somebody already
# has, so the register would hold the very data it exists to prove it deleted.
# Salting with a deployment secret closes that.
#   pnpm exec convex env set PURGE_HASH_SALT "$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
# Distinct per deployment, and never committed. Rotating it makes earlier
# entries unanswerable — they remain proof that a session was purged, but you
# can no longer ask whose. Unset, every erasure path throws
# `purge_hash_salt_not_configured`, deliberately: a register that silently
# wrote the unsalted digest would look correct and carry none of the property.

# ─── Media origin for the CSP (web server, NOT Convex) ─────────────────────
# The only object-store setting that does not live on the Convex deployment:
# the Content-Security-Policy is served by the TanStack Start server, which
# never talks to the bucket. Set it on the Scalingo app (or here for
# `pnpm dev`) to the origin the signed URLs point at:
MEDIA_ORIGIN=
#   e.g. https://interw-media.s3.fr-par.scw.cloud
# Unset, `media-src` falls back to `https:` and video still plays — set it to
# pin playback to the one host it should come from. See KNOWN_ISSUES.md
# § "The template's HTTP headers denied the camera".

# ─── AI providers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Transcription runs on Mistral directly (European provider; candidate
# recordings are the most sensitive data here). Evaluation runs on OpenRouter
# so the model can change without a redeploy. Both live in the Convex env:
#   pnpm exec convex env set MISTRAL_API_KEY ...
#   pnpm exec convex env set OPENROUTER_API_KEY ...
# → Mistral:    https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys
# → OpenRouter: https://openrouter.ai/keys

# ─── Resend delivery webhook (optional but recommended) ────────────────────
# Lets Interw tell a bounced invitation apart from a candidate who simply has
# not opened it yet. In the Resend dashboard, add a webhook pointing at
#   https://<your-convex-site-url>/resend-webhook
# then store the signing secret on the Convex deployment:
#   pnpm exec convex env set RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET whsec_...
# The endpoint is public by necessity; the signature is the only thing between
# it and forged bounce reports, so it will reject everything without this set.
